{"book":10,"chapter":19,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE LANGUAGE IN DEPTH / CHAPTER 19","slides":[{"title":"Duck and contract","sub":"Chapter 19 · Build-time checks","short":"Intro","main":"Rust checks “does the type do this?” at build time, Python at run time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python: duck","Rust: contract","When the error"],"captions":["In Python any object with the right method works, but the check runs when the line executes","In Rust the requirement is in the signature: any T that implements Shape works, and the compiler checks it","A Python error surfaces on the user, a Rust error at build time"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["def total(shapes):","    return sum(s.area() for s in shapes)","","total([Circle(1), 42])  # 💥 at run time"],"hl":[3],"bad":[3],"lang":"plain","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Shape { fn area(&self) -> f64; }","","fn total<T: Shape>(v: &[T]) -> f64 {","    v.iter().map(|s| s.area()).sum()","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":100.0,"y":50.0,"w":140.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Python: at run time","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":100.0,"y":100.0,"w":140.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Rust: at build time","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"bar","id":"b1","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":24.0,"hh":40.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"red","text":""},{"t":"bar","id":"b2","x":330.0,"y":70.0,"w":24.0,"hh":8.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"green","text":""},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"the earlier the error, the cheaper","size":9.5}]],"cues":[15.3,25.1]}]},{"title":"Generic functions","sub":"T and bounds","short":"Generics","main":"The caller supplies T; only the trait bound allows operations on T.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Type parameter","No bound","With a trait"],"captions":["The function is written once: T is any type name the caller supplies","But two T cannot be compared: not every type has “greater”, so the compiler refuses","The bound T: PartialOrd says only comparable types fit, and the error goes away"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn largest<T>(v: &[T]) -> &T {","    // ...","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":17.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":95.0,"y":120.0,"w":104.0,"h":24.0,"text":"largest(&[1, 5, 3])","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":245.0,"y":120.0,"w":116.0,"h":24.0,"text":"largest(&[\"a\", \"z\"])","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["fn largest<T>(v: &[T]) -> &T {","    let mut m = &v[0];","    for x in v { if x > m { m = x; } }","    m","}"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"w":330.0,"h":30.0,"text":"error[E0369]: binary operation `>` cannot be\napplied to type `&T`","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn largest<T: PartialOrd>(v: &[T]) -> &T {","    let mut m = &v[0];","    for x in v { if x > m { m = x; } }","    m","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"now i32, f64, &str, String… all fit","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.6,23.1]}]},{"title":"Trait and impl","sub":"Behavior apart from data","short":"Trait","main":"A trait is a set of methods; the impl is written separately; no foreign trait for a foreign type.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["trait","impl for types","Orphan rule"],"captions":["A trait is a set of methods a type promises to provide: closest to a Python ABC or Protocol","The impl is separate from the type: Circle and Rect implement one trait, and you can add your trait even to a foreign type","You cannot implement a foreign trait for a foreign type: two libraries could not agree"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Shape {","    fn area(&self) -> f64;","    fn name(&self) -> String;","}"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":36.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"trait Shape","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"impl for Circle","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":112.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"impl for Rect","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":240.0,"y1":98.0,"x2":200.0,"y2":50.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"crate A: impl\nDisplay for Vec","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"crate B: impl\nDisplay for Vec","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"x","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"✕","tone":"red","size":18.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"you must own the trait or the type","size":9.5}]],"cues":[9.3,27.5]}]},{"title":"Default methods","sub":"Ready methods and supertraits","short":"Defaults","main":"The type writes the required methods, the rest comes ready; a trait has no fields.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Required and ready","Override","Supertrait"],"captions":["The type writes the required method; methods with a body in the trait come free, as in Iterator","Any ready method can be overridden if the type has a faster way","A trait can require another: to be a Shape, a type must implement Debug, but a trait has no data"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["trait Shape {","    fn area(&self) -> f64;       // required","    fn describe(&self) -> String {","        format!(\"area {:.1}\", self.area())","    }","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Shape for Square {","    fn area(&self) -> f64 { self.0 * self.0 }","    fn describe(&self) -> String {","        \"square\".into()   // custom\"","    }","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["trait Shape: Debug {","    fn area(&self) -> f64;","}","// no fields, no data inheritance"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[11.4,24.9]}]},{"title":"Standard traits","sub":"Debug, Clone, Ord, Add…","short":"Standard","main":"Printing, copying, ordering, and operators are all traits; many come via derive.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Printing and copies","Equality and order","Operators"],"captions":["Debug and Display print, Clone and Copy copy, Default builds a default value","PartialEq and Eq: equality, PartialOrd and Ord: order, Hash: hash; most come via derive","An operator is a trait method: a + b becomes Add::add(a, b), so complex numbers read as formulas"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":54.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Debug","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":120.0,"y":70.0,"w":54.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Display","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":54.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Clone","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":240.0,"y":70.0,"w":54.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Copy","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":54.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Default","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"{:?}   {}   .clone()   =   Default::default()","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":56.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"PartialEq","tone":"blue","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":118.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Eq","tone":"blue","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"PartialOrd","tone":"blue","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":242.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Ord","tone":"blue","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":304.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Hash","tone":"blue","size":7.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash)]","size":8.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["impl Add for Complex {","    type Output = Complex;","    fn add(self, o: Complex) -> Complex {","        Complex::new(self.re + o.re, self.im + o.im)","    }","}","let z = a + b;   // Add::add(a, b)"],"hl":[6],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":15.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[15.3,27.0]}]},{"title":"Monomorphization","sub":"A copy per type","short":"Monomorphization","main":"Generics are free at run time and cost code size and build time.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One source","A copy per type","The price"],"captions":["A generic function is written once, but it is a template, not finished code","For each type it is called with, the compiler makes a separate copy tuned to it and calls it directly","Speed of hand-copied code; the price is program size, instruction cache load, and build time"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":180.0,"h":40.0,"text":"fn largest<T>(…)","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"one template","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"largest<T>","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":240.0,"y":36.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"largest::<i32>","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"largest::<f64>","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":240.0,"y":104.0,"w":130.0,"h":26.0,"text":"largest::<&str>","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":126.0,"y1":46.0,"x2":174.0,"y2":38.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":126.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":174.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":126.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":174.0,"y2":102.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"bar","id":"s1","x":90.0,"y":120.0,"w":40.0,"hh":30.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":""},{"t":"bar","id":"s2","x":210.0,"y":120.0,"w":40.0,"hh":80.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"yellow","text":""},{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":90.0,"y":140.0,"text":"code size","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":210.0,"y":140.0,"text":"code size","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"a1","x":90.0,"y":18.0,"text":"dyn","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"a2","x":210.0,"y":18.0,"text":"generics","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":310.0,"y":80.0,"text":"fast,\nbut bigger","size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.4,25.1]}]},{"title":"where and impl Trait","sub":"Short bound syntax","short":"where","main":"where reads better than long brackets; impl Trait hides the concrete type.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["where","impl Trait in an argument","impl Trait in a result"],"captions":["With many bounds, move them to a where block: it reads well and avoids a long list in brackets","In an argument, “impl Trait” means “any type with this trait”: the same monomorphic code, shorter","In a result it hides the concrete type, such as a long iterator, promising only “something iterable”"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["fn show_all<T, U>(a: &[T], b: U)","where","    T: Display + Clone,","    U: Into<String>,","{ ... }"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn print_all(items: &[impl Display]) {","    for i in items { println!(\"{i}\"); }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"= fn print_all<T: Display>(items: &[T])","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":46.0,"lines":["fn evens(limit: u32) -> impl Iterator<Item = u32> {","    (0..limit).filter(|n| n % 2 == 0)","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"type Filter<Range<u32>, closure> is hidden","size":9.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[12.7,19.7]}]},{"title":"dyn Trait","sub":"Trait objects and vtable","short":"dyn","main":"Box<dyn Trait> is 16 bytes: data and method table; the call is indirect.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Mixed list","Fat pointer","Method table"],"captions":["Vec<Box<dyn Shape>> holds circles and rectangles together: the type is known only at run time","Box<dyn Shape> is two words on the stack: data address and virtual method table address (16 bytes)","The table holds drop, size, alignment, and method pointers; a call is an indirect jump, like a function pointer in C"],"frames":[[{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":20.0,"text":"Vec<Box<dyn Shape>>","size":9.5,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Circle\nr = 1.0","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Rect\n2 × 3","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Square\n4","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"on the heap: different types and sizes","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":44.0,"text":"Box<dyn Shape>\ndata · vtable","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":44.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"data: Circle","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"vtable Circle","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":126.0,"y1":64.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":46.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":126.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":98.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":70.0,"y":112.0,"text":"16 bytes","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"v0","x":130.0,"y":30.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"drop_in_place","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v1","x":130.0,"y":54.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"size = 8","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v2","x":130.0,"y":78.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"align = 8","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v3","x":130.0,"y":102.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"area → Circle::area","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v4","x":130.0,"y":126.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"name → Circle::name","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":245.0,"y1":102.0,"x2":280.0,"y2":102.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":300.0,"y":102.0,"text":"call [vtable+24]","size":8.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[10.1,22.6]}]},{"title":"Static or dynamic","sub":"Direct and indirect call","short":"Choice","main":"Generics are faster, dyn is more flexible: use dyn for mixed types and plugins.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Direct call","Via the table","What to choose"],"captions":["Generics: the call is known at build time, a direct jump that can be inlined and optimized","Trait object: the method address is read from the table at run time, an indirect jump that cannot be inlined","Start with generics, use dyn for mixed types or plugins; not every trait can be made an object"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"call","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":96.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":144.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"area_circle","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"call area_circle  (may be inlined)","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":28.0,"text":"call","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":80.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":114.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":150.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":28.0,"text":"vtable","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":180.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Circle::area","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"call [vtable+24]  — indirect","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":44.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"generics: speed","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":78.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"dyn: mixed types","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"dyn: plugins","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":78.0,"w":130.0,"h":50.0,"text":"not allowed in dyn:\nSelf by value,\ngeneric methods","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.9,24.0]}]},{"title":"Associated types","sub":"Iterator and constants","short":"Assoc","main":"One Item per impl; next is enough, adapters come on their own.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Iterator","Your own iterator","Constants in a trait"],"captions":["The associated type Item is declared inside the trait: one per impl, and no extra parameter in signatures","For the struct Fib, the method next is enough: map, filter, take, and sum come ready","A trait can declare a constant too: each type has its own SIDES, known at build time and taking no space in the data"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Iterator {","    type Item;","    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<Self::Item>;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":26.0,"lines":["struct Fib { a: u64, b: u64 }","impl Iterator for Fib {","    type Item = u64;","    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<u64> {","        let r = self.a;","        (self.a, self.b) = (self.b, self.a + self.b);","        Some(r)","    }","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":14.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Polygon {","    const SIDES: u32;","}","impl Polygon for Triangle { const SIDES: u32 = 3; }","// Triangle::SIDES == 3"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[8.6,24.6]}]},{"title":"Generic structs","sub":"Stack<T>, conditional impl","short":"Stack<T>","main":"impl<T: Display> adds methods only where they make sense.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Stack<T>","Conditional impl","Blanket impl"],"captions":["Stack<i32> and Stack<String> are different types with different layouts: the compiler substitutes T and recomputes the size","The impl<T: Display> block adds methods only for T that can be printed","“For every T: Display implement ToString”: one blanket impl gives to_string on numbers, strings, and your types"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct Stack<T> { items: Vec<T> }","impl<T> Stack<T> {","    fn push(&mut self, x: T) { self.items.push(x) }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":350.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":110.0,"y":128.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Stack<i32>: 24 bytes","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":128.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Stack<String>","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl<T: Display> Stack<T> {","    fn show(&self) -> String { ... }","}","// Stack<Vec<u8>>::show is not available"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl<T: Display> ToString for T {","    fn to_string(&self) -> String { ... }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"5.to_string()   \"hi\".to_string()   point.to_string()","size":8.5,"mono":true}]],"cues":[17.1,23.9]}]},{"title":"Conversions","sub":"From, TryFrom, FromStr","short":"From","main":"From/Into, TryFrom, FromStr, AsRef are the shared language of Rust libraries.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["From and Into","TryFrom","FromStr and parse"],"captions":["impl From<A> for B gives a free a.into(); the ? operator uses From to convert errors","TryFrom is the same but can fail: u8::try_from(300) returns Err","FromStr enables \"…\".parse::<MyType>(); AsRef accepts “anything string- or slice-like”"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ParseIntError","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"AppError::Parse","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":96.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":52.0,"text":"From::from","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"a.into()   and   ?","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let a = u8::try_from(200)?;   // Ok(200)","let b = u8::try_from(300);    // Err"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"10,20\"","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":100.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":120.0,"y":54.0,"text":".parse()","size":9.0,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Point { x: 10, y: 20 }","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"impl FromStr for Point","size":9.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[9.2,21.5]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Generics + traits + bounds; next, closures and iterators.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three tools","The price","Next"],"captions":["Generics write code once, traits describe behavior, bounds tie them together","Monomorphization: speed for size; dyn: mixed types for an indirect call","Next, closures and iterators: built on these same traits (Fn, FnMut, FnOnce, Iterator)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"generics\nT","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"traits\nbehavior","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"bounds\nT: Trait","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":56.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"static: fast, more code","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":100.0,"y":96.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"dyn: flexible, indirect call","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"text":"16 bytes\nfor &dyn","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let add = |a, b| a + b;","let evens: Vec<_> = v.iter()","    .filter(|x| *x % 2 == 0).collect();"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"text":"closures and iterators","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[7.2,19.5]}]}]}